  "reasoning": "Ranking blends recent tier-1 results with roster stability, weighting the Esports World Cup most heavily since it included 15 of 16 TI teams. Top tier: Team Vision (EWC champion, DreamLeague 29 winner, dominant map record), Team Yandex (Wallachia 7 + BLAST Slam VII, EWC third), BoomBoys (Wallachia 8, EWC runner-up), Team Spirit (clean EU qualifier, EWC 5th-8th), Team Falcons (defending champions, unchanged roster, but a mediocre 2026 and a 0-2 EWC quarterfinal exit to Vici). Swiss is high-variance: a 4-0 run needs four Bo1/Bo3 wins, so no team exceeds ~12% for w4_l0, and even the best have roughly a 30% miss chance. Second tier is tightly packed: Liquid, Vici, Aurora and Xtreme are separated by noise. Vici's EWC fourth is real but partly bracket-dependent; Xtreme's 13th-16th is worse than their form elsewhere, so I regress both toward the middle. 1win and Nigma sit just under even odds. LGD are downgraded meaningfully: losing TaiLung days before the event and inserting a stand-in who hasn't played since 2024 disrupts drafting and mid-lane synergy more than Topson's pedigree compensates. OG and Resilience are live but unproven at this level; Resilience has almost no tier-1 sample, which widens their distribution both ways. GamerLegion and HULIGANI are the clearest weak entries, both bottom-tier at EWC, and carry most of the 0-4 mass. Championship equity concentrates on the five strongest, but I keep it flatter than group-stage strength because a Bo5 double-elimination bracket rewards depth and any of ten teams could win. Total spread reflects that no favorite exceeds ~16%.",
